1
00:00:01,141 --> 00:00:04,981
Do you happen to know anything about my father's accident?

2
00:00:05,511 --> 00:00:07,951
What kind of accident it was and how it happened...

3
00:00:08,651 --> 00:00:12,081
Well, all I know is that it was a car accident.

4
00:00:12,491 --> 00:00:17,791
At night, a speeding car tried to pass your father's car and...

5
00:00:18,491 --> 00:00:19,731
What?

6
00:00:22,931 --> 00:00:23,931
Chief Seo.

7
00:00:24,261 --> 00:00:25,361
Team Leader Ko.

8
00:00:26,171 --> 00:00:27,231
You didn't go to work?

9
00:00:27,671 --> 00:00:30,541
Yes, I'm heading in soon. Are you here to see Grandfather?

10
00:00:30,701 --> 00:00:33,171
Yes. I saw him, and now I'm on my way to work.

11
00:00:33,341 --> 00:00:34,611
Okay, please go ahead.

12
00:00:34,811 --> 00:00:36,811
I have something to ask Secretary Ju.

13
00:00:37,111 --> 00:00:39,181
I see. I'm on my way to work anyway.

14
00:00:39,581 --> 00:00:40,811
I can wait, and we can go together.

15
00:00:41,011 --> 00:00:44,251
It's all right. You go ahead. This might take a while.

16
00:00:45,081 --> 00:00:46,091
All right, then.

17
00:00:47,091 --> 00:00:48,991
- Take care, Chief Seo. - Yes.

18
00:00:50,861 --> 00:00:53,361
Then do you know anything about the driver...

19
00:00:53,361 --> 00:00:54,561
who caused the accident?

20
00:00:55,091 --> 00:00:57,431
I think I heard he turned himself. and for involuntary manslaughter,

21
00:00:57,501 --> 00:01:00,131
he was sentenced to five years.

22
00:01:02,601 --> 00:01:03,801
Hey, why are you still here?

23
00:01:04,471 --> 00:01:06,071
Yes. I'm leaving.

24
00:01:10,341 --> 00:01:12,141
I don't know anything else.

25
00:01:12,451 --> 00:01:17,321
But Gyeol, did you really lose all your memories from back then?

26
00:01:18,351 --> 00:01:19,391
Yes.

27
00:01:20,391 --> 00:01:23,021
Then why are you suddenly curious?

28
00:01:23,191 --> 00:01:25,461
It's not like it's a good memory.

29
00:01:26,791 --> 00:01:28,631
Thank you. I should get going.

30
00:01:28,761 --> 00:01:31,001
What? You came all this way, and you're leaving...

31
00:01:31,001 --> 00:01:33,131
- without seeing the Chairman? - I have to get straight to work.

32
00:01:33,131 --> 00:01:35,371
I'll see Grandfather next time I visit.

33
00:01:37,301 --> 00:01:38,371
Hey, but...

34
00:01:40,911 --> 00:01:42,881
Why is he suddenly asking about that accident?

35
00:01:45,241 --> 00:01:46,681
Gyeol was here?

36
00:01:47,811 --> 00:01:48,851
Yes.

37
00:01:49,081 --> 00:01:52,021
He asked me about his father's accident 25 years ago.

38
00:01:52,081 --> 00:01:54,021
He asked if I knew anything about it.

39
00:01:54,451 --> 00:01:56,461
What? Why all of a sudden?

40
00:01:57,461 --> 00:02:00,191
It seems Gyeol has lost all his memories of that time.

41
00:02:01,291 --> 00:02:03,701
I wonder if he suddenly remembered something.

42
00:02:05,771 --> 00:02:08,601
I have to go prune some branches, so I'll be on my way.

43
00:02:08,671 --> 00:02:11,041
- All right. Thank you. - Yes.

44
00:02:14,611 --> 00:02:15,641
What's wrong?

45
00:02:16,311 --> 00:02:17,981
Is something worrying you?

46
00:02:19,181 --> 00:02:20,751
No, it's nothing to worry about.

47
00:02:22,081 --> 00:02:25,321
Do you remember when Gyeol was a child?

48
00:02:26,391 --> 00:02:30,461
The day he came to this house and started talking again.

49
00:02:31,291 --> 00:02:34,831
Of course. How could I ever forget that day?

50
00:02:39,871 --> 00:02:40,901
Dad.

51
00:02:42,071 --> 00:02:43,971
Gyeol.

52
00:02:45,201 --> 00:02:48,071
Dad. Dad!

53
00:02:48,811 --> 00:02:50,741
Dad.

54
00:02:52,441 --> 00:02:54,051
Dad.

55
00:02:54,851 --> 00:02:59,821
I think Gyeol is finally ready to face the pain he has kept...

56
00:03:01,491 --> 00:03:05,321
- buried deep inside for so long. - Oh, dear.

57
00:03:06,191 --> 00:03:08,861
I just hope he doesn't get hurt.

58
00:03:10,801 --> 00:03:13,971
Father, Mother. Is there anything you need?

59
00:03:14,331 --> 00:03:15,601
No. Why do you ask?

60
00:03:15,971 --> 00:03:19,541
Well, if you think about it, I'm sure there must be something.

61
00:03:19,911 --> 00:03:22,441
I just really want to do something for you.

62
00:03:22,711 --> 00:03:25,711
I was thinking of calling Yeon Soon. We can all have lunch together.

63
00:03:25,951 --> 00:03:28,481
What? You're seeing Ms. Kang Yeon Ja again?

64
00:03:30,251 --> 00:03:32,891
Yes. You should call her.

65
00:03:33,251 --> 00:03:34,791
You've missed 50 years of being with her.

66
00:03:34,851 --> 00:03:38,521
So you should see each other as much as possible. Of course.

67
00:03:39,091 --> 00:03:40,561
From now on,

68
00:03:40,561 --> 00:03:42,331
you will treat each other with the proper respect.

69
00:03:43,231 --> 00:03:47,101
- She's your sister-in-law. - What? My sister-in-law?

70
00:03:48,601 --> 00:03:50,201
If she's my sister-in-law...

71
00:03:50,941 --> 00:03:54,371
Oh, then she's like my "Sis."

72
00:03:54,811 --> 00:03:57,481
Who calls their sister-in-law "Sis" these days?

73
00:03:58,081 --> 00:03:59,311
Just act the way you always have.

74
00:03:59,611 --> 00:04:02,411
No, I can't. She's my esteemed sister-in-law.

75
00:04:04,021 --> 00:04:05,151
Thank you, General Director.

76
00:04:05,481 --> 00:04:07,751
- Why are you suddenly thanking me? - What?

77
00:04:08,321 --> 00:04:10,791
Well, I took a long vacation for personal reasons,

78
00:04:10,861 --> 00:04:13,691
and you were so understanding....

79
00:04:13,761 --> 00:04:15,901
Han Ji Hun, please upload the latest version...

80
00:04:15,961 --> 00:04:17,231
of our team's Joy upgrade.

81
00:04:17,761 --> 00:04:19,831
What? Oh, yes.

82
00:04:22,531 --> 00:04:24,101
The third competition will include aspects...

83
00:04:24,171 --> 00:04:25,541
of the first and second competitions,

84
00:04:25,601 --> 00:04:27,371
and most importantly, the site selection.

85
00:04:27,871 --> 00:04:29,641
Since this is a comprehensive evaluation,

86
00:04:29,781 --> 00:04:31,481
I hope you all will approach it with the mindset of...

87
00:04:31,481 --> 00:04:32,551
a completely fresh start.

88
00:04:32,651 --> 00:04:33,951
- Yes, understood. - Yes, understood.

89
00:04:35,011 --> 00:04:37,081
By the way, where is everyone from Team Two?

90
00:04:37,221 --> 00:04:39,121
Oh, Team Leader Ko is on his way back...

91
00:04:39,181 --> 00:04:42,291
from some off-site business. Mr. Kim is in the records room.

92
00:04:42,551 --> 00:04:43,561
Off-site business?

93
00:04:44,091 --> 00:04:47,461
- Everyone, keep up the good work. - Yes.

94
00:04:47,591 --> 00:04:50,131
Our team has a meeting, so we will head out first.

95
00:04:50,401 --> 00:04:51,501
Okay, good work.

96
00:05:00,241 --> 00:05:01,841
Can we talk for a minute?

97
00:05:03,041 --> 00:05:05,211
The meeting is in ten minutes, so get to the point.

98
00:05:09,521 --> 00:05:12,221
I'm truly sorry. For trying to copy your file.

99
00:05:12,321 --> 00:05:16,021
And for showing that video during the competition.

100
00:05:16,291 --> 00:05:17,291
All of it.

101
00:05:18,321 --> 00:05:20,831
And thank you for covering for me.

102
00:05:21,331 --> 00:05:23,801
I have not forgiven you, Han Ji Hun.

103
00:05:24,861 --> 00:05:25,971
What do you mean?

104
00:05:26,431 --> 00:05:29,171
I let it slide because I wanted to face off one last time...

105
00:05:29,401 --> 00:05:32,101
against that passionate and capable senior I used to know...

106
00:05:32,101 --> 00:05:34,741
when we first founded Lucky Joy and were developing Joy.

107
00:05:37,341 --> 00:05:38,781
Are you giving me a chance?

108
00:05:38,841 --> 00:05:41,451
Yes. This is the last chance I am giving you, so make it count.

109
00:05:43,321 --> 00:05:44,321
Okay.

110
00:05:45,521 --> 00:05:47,221
I understand what you mean.

111
00:05:48,151 --> 00:05:50,091
Thank you. I will fight with all I have got.

112
00:05:51,521 --> 00:05:53,091
As for Team Leader Ko, make sure you separately...

113
00:05:54,191 --> 00:05:55,691
apologise to him sincerely.

114
00:05:56,231 --> 00:05:59,731
Using someone's weakness was a truly cowardly thing to do.

115
00:06:01,101 --> 00:06:03,371
Yes, I am ashamed of myself.

116
00:06:04,771 --> 00:06:05,801
I will be sure to apologise.

117
00:06:13,981 --> 00:06:16,421
Where did you go without eating breakfast?

118
00:06:17,251 --> 00:06:19,691
To my family's home. I went to see Secretary Ju.

119
00:06:19,851 --> 00:06:21,621
Secretary Ju? Why so suddenly...

120
00:06:22,451 --> 00:06:24,891
I suddenly remembered that Grandfather and Secretary Ju...

121
00:06:24,891 --> 00:06:26,691
came to my father's funeral to pay their respects.

122
00:06:27,291 --> 00:06:30,461
So I asked if he happened to know anything...

123
00:06:30,461 --> 00:06:33,001
- about my father's accident. - Did you find anything out?

124
00:06:33,671 --> 00:06:35,901
No. Grandfather and Secretary Ju rushed there...

125
00:06:35,971 --> 00:06:37,771
after hearing the news of the accident.

126
00:06:39,201 --> 00:06:42,071
From now on, let's find things out slowly.

127
00:06:42,141 --> 00:06:43,411
Let us not be too hasty.

128
00:06:43,681 --> 00:06:47,851
You are right. We should not rush. I was a bit impatient today.

129
00:06:48,311 --> 00:06:50,851
Oh, please keep your schedule free after work today.

130
00:06:51,221 --> 00:06:52,791
Why? Is something the matter?

131
00:06:52,791 --> 00:06:54,821
Yes. Asking you on a first date.

132
00:06:55,191 --> 00:06:57,991
What? A date? But we are together every day.

133
00:06:59,121 --> 00:07:00,191
I am sorry I am late.

134
00:07:00,831 --> 00:07:02,161
I was gathering some materials related to...

135
00:07:02,161 --> 00:07:03,531
selecting overseas sites for the Retirement Community.

136
00:07:03,601 --> 00:07:06,271
- Oh, I see. - Yes.

137
00:07:06,601 --> 00:07:09,101
Site selection is the most important part of the third competition,

138
00:07:09,171 --> 00:07:11,271
so this is very useful data. Good work.

139
00:07:11,341 --> 00:07:13,411
Now, only the final competition is left.

140
00:07:13,471 --> 00:07:14,471
Let's do our best.

141
00:07:15,911 --> 00:07:17,011
Is that lunchbox for me?

142
00:07:17,681 --> 00:07:19,781
Why would this be for you?

143
00:07:19,781 --> 00:07:21,051
It's for your maternal grandmother...

144
00:07:23,281 --> 00:07:24,281
Are you wearing makeup?

145
00:07:25,851 --> 00:07:27,451
And why is your skirt so short?

146
00:07:27,821 --> 00:07:29,991
Why? You said I looked pretty.

147
00:07:29,991 --> 00:07:31,891
You told me to always dress like this.

148
00:07:32,421 --> 00:07:34,791
Go upstairs, change into the sweats you usually wear,

149
00:07:34,791 --> 00:07:37,501
- and come back down. - No. Why?

150
00:07:38,201 --> 00:07:40,531
Come to think of it, I knew you had changed for a while now.

151
00:07:41,331 --> 00:07:44,471
Do you like him? That pretty boy?

152
00:07:44,641 --> 00:07:48,111
What are you talking about? As if I like someone.

153
00:07:48,241 --> 00:07:50,141
Oh, look at you stuttering. It must be true.

154
00:07:50,211 --> 00:07:52,581
What are you talking about? I am swamped with my webtoon.

155
00:07:53,781 --> 00:07:56,551
Anyway, when are you free?

156
00:07:56,821 --> 00:07:59,181
Mom, when am I ever free?

157
00:07:59,181 --> 00:08:00,951
Every day it is the series and everything else.

158
00:08:01,721 --> 00:08:03,861
But why do you ask?

159
00:08:04,591 --> 00:08:07,231
Your maternal grandmother wants to see you kids.

160
00:08:07,831 --> 00:08:10,601
She has seen Eun Ae, but she has never properly met...

161
00:08:10,601 --> 00:08:12,661
you, Eun Hyung, and Bit Na.

162
00:08:12,801 --> 00:08:14,731
Well, I'd like to meet her too.

163
00:08:15,071 --> 00:08:17,241
Oh, aren't they having a living funeral soon?

164
00:08:17,301 --> 00:08:19,441
- We can see her then. - That's a separate occasion.

165
00:08:19,441 --> 00:08:21,211
She said she wants to spend some quality time...

166
00:08:21,211 --> 00:08:23,011
with her grandchildren before that.

167
00:08:23,511 --> 00:08:24,981
So try to make some time soon.

168
00:08:25,041 --> 00:08:27,781
Okay, then. I'll have to coordinate with Eun Hyung to go and see her.

169
00:08:28,451 --> 00:08:29,981
I'll talk to him tonight, and we'll set a date.

170
00:08:30,321 --> 00:08:35,221
- Okay, then. - Have a good time with Grandma.

171
00:08:35,221 --> 00:08:37,021
Make up for lost time and be a good daughter.

172
00:08:37,261 --> 00:08:39,421
Oh, please. You just worry about yourself.

173
00:08:39,421 --> 00:08:41,161
You know what'll happen if you break your curfew, right?

174
00:08:41,161 --> 00:08:44,201
That's so lame. A curfew? Seriously?

175
00:08:44,331 --> 00:08:45,661
I'm heading out.

176
00:08:54,371 --> 00:08:56,181
Yes, it's me.

177
00:08:57,841 --> 00:09:00,211
I'll stop by for a bit later.

178
00:09:01,751 --> 00:09:04,951
Oh, I just thought I'd make you some lunch.

179
00:09:18,531 --> 00:09:20,101
No, that's not it.

180
00:09:21,001 --> 00:09:22,001
Oh, wait.

181
00:09:24,501 --> 00:09:26,941
Five. Four.

182
00:09:27,311 --> 00:09:28,311
Three.

183
00:09:28,811 --> 00:09:29,811
Two.

184
00:09:30,511 --> 00:09:31,511
One.

185
00:09:32,211 --> 00:09:33,611
Oh, you're here?

186
00:09:35,781 --> 00:09:37,551
Hye Ji.

187
00:09:38,151 --> 00:09:39,851
No, I mean, Hye Ji what are you doing here?

188
00:09:40,091 --> 00:09:42,391
Why? Are you disappointed to see me?

189
00:09:42,751 --> 00:09:44,621
No, no, it's not that.

190
00:09:44,621 --> 00:09:46,361
I haven't heard from you in a while,

191
00:09:46,491 --> 00:09:49,261
so you showing up all of a sudden just surprised me.

192
00:09:49,601 --> 00:09:52,031
I've been so busy with my final exams.

193
00:09:52,361 --> 00:09:54,331
I'm sorry for not keeping in touch.

194
00:09:54,501 --> 00:09:55,971
Oh, no, it's fine. Really.

195
00:09:56,241 --> 00:09:59,041
Not at all. You have nothing to be sorry about.

196
00:09:59,811 --> 00:10:01,811
Happy Kiss Day to us.

197
00:10:02,241 --> 00:10:03,941
Excuse me? Kiss Day?

198
00:10:04,011 --> 00:10:08,511
Yes, it's Kiss Day, the 44th day since we met,

199
00:10:08,751 --> 00:10:10,751
and it's when you're supposed to have your first kiss.

200
00:10:10,951 --> 00:10:12,451
Gosh.

201
00:10:14,591 --> 00:10:16,291
Oh, Eun Nim, perfect timing.

202
00:10:18,191 --> 00:10:21,491
It's our Kiss Day today. Can you take a picture for us?

203
00:10:21,761 --> 00:10:23,531
What? Kiss Day?

204
00:10:25,461 --> 00:10:26,501
Sure, why not.

205
00:10:27,401 --> 00:10:29,471
Hey, no, no, no.

206
00:10:29,741 --> 00:10:31,201
I mean, what is all this about a Kiss Day?

207
00:10:31,271 --> 00:10:32,341
What are you talking about?

208
00:10:33,111 --> 00:10:34,111
Hurry up and take the picture.

209
00:10:34,511 --> 00:10:35,511
But...

210
00:10:46,451 --> 00:10:48,151
Oh, come on, wait a second.

211
00:10:50,191 --> 00:10:52,621
Hye Ji, this isn't happening. Okay?

212
00:10:54,031 --> 00:10:55,131
Okay, look.

213
00:10:55,131 --> 00:10:56,961
Yes, I might have said "okay" or "deal..."

214
00:10:56,961 --> 00:10:58,431
when I was drunk,

215
00:10:58,501 --> 00:11:00,071
and I am very, very sorry about that.

216
00:11:00,801 --> 00:11:04,271
But did we ever agree to date? Have we even talked on the phone?

217
00:11:04,671 --> 00:11:06,911
This is purely your misunderstanding, Hye Ji.

218
00:11:07,911 --> 00:11:10,141
Is it because of Eun Nim?

219
00:11:10,641 --> 00:11:12,981
- What? - Hey, Hye Ji.

220
00:11:13,481 --> 00:11:14,911
Writer Seo, do you perhaps...

221
00:11:17,051 --> 00:11:18,651
Yes, that is correct.

222
00:11:20,551 --> 00:11:22,121
I have feelings for Writer Jo Eun Nim.

223
00:11:22,551 --> 00:11:23,621
Bung Woo.

224
00:11:24,191 --> 00:11:25,261
Yes, Bung Nim.

225
00:11:26,021 --> 00:11:29,131
Now that it has come to this, I will make my intentions clear.

226
00:11:30,031 --> 00:11:31,101
I like you.

227
00:11:31,901 --> 00:11:32,901
Bung Nim.

228
00:11:33,701 --> 00:11:34,701
What?

229
00:11:35,271 --> 00:11:36,441
Bung Woo, Bung Nim?

230
00:11:37,741 --> 00:11:39,571
Jo Eun Nim, tell me.

231
00:11:40,041 --> 00:11:41,841
Do you like Writer Seo too? Is that it?

232
00:11:41,911 --> 00:11:44,581
Well, I'm not really sure,

233
00:11:45,081 --> 00:11:47,111
but then again, I think I might.

234
00:11:48,281 --> 00:11:49,281
So,

235
00:11:49,751 --> 00:11:52,221
have I been fanning the flames of your little romance?

236
00:11:52,281 --> 00:11:54,551
- Adding fuel to the fire? - Hye Ji, don't misunderstand.

237
00:11:54,821 --> 00:11:57,061
I'm not even sure about my own feelings yet.

238
00:12:00,661 --> 00:12:03,931
Whatever. Good luck, you two. You actually look good together.

239
00:12:04,361 --> 00:12:05,361
What?

240
00:12:06,731 --> 00:12:10,241
Honestly, I was too busy studying to date.

241
00:12:10,371 --> 00:12:11,401
So this is for the best.

242
00:12:11,971 --> 00:12:14,171
I'm just going to focus on the national exam now,

243
00:12:14,171 --> 00:12:15,311
so you two have a lovely romance.

244
00:12:15,911 --> 00:12:16,911
Well then.

245
00:12:17,381 --> 00:12:18,411
Hye Ji.

246
00:12:22,581 --> 00:12:23,751
So...

247
00:12:25,781 --> 00:12:28,821
I already told you that I like you, Bung Nim.

248
00:12:29,991 --> 00:12:31,361
What about you, Bung Nim?

249
00:12:32,791 --> 00:12:33,791
Do you not like me?

250
00:12:36,431 --> 00:12:38,431
No, I don't dislike you.

251
00:12:39,531 --> 00:12:41,201
Does that mean you like me?

252
00:12:41,631 --> 00:12:44,041
No, it's not that I like you.

253
00:12:44,541 --> 00:12:45,741
I just said I don't dislike you.

254
00:12:46,201 --> 00:12:47,871
That's the same thing.

255
00:12:49,341 --> 00:12:51,581
Bung Woo, Bung Nim, you're my witnesses, okay?

256
00:12:51,641 --> 00:12:54,011
No, wait. You're not witnesses. You're the proof.

257
00:12:54,151 --> 00:12:55,181
That's not it.

258
00:12:55,911 --> 00:12:58,121
I'm telling you I'm not sure yet.

259
00:13:01,291 --> 00:13:02,691
Go back to work.

260
00:13:05,221 --> 00:13:06,221
Okay.

261
00:13:07,961 --> 00:13:11,031
You're making cold noodles? That's so much work.

262
00:13:11,301 --> 00:13:12,901
It's no trouble.

263
00:13:12,961 --> 00:13:14,771
I made the broth yesterday and put it in the fridge to chill,

264
00:13:14,831 --> 00:13:16,441
and I also prepared all the toppings.

265
00:13:16,741 --> 00:13:18,371
I just need to boil the noodles.

266
00:13:18,871 --> 00:13:20,871
I was planning on making lunch.

267
00:13:21,671 --> 00:13:24,011
Oh my, you're here, Sister-in-law?

268
00:13:24,811 --> 00:13:26,611
Sister-in-law?

269
00:13:27,451 --> 00:13:29,351
Did you just call me sister-in-law?

270
00:13:29,511 --> 00:13:33,081
Yes, you're my husband's sister, so that makes you my sister-in-law.

271
00:13:33,081 --> 00:13:34,121
And I'm your brother's wife.

272
00:13:34,351 --> 00:13:36,521
So, from now on, instead of calling me...

273
00:13:36,591 --> 00:13:37,821
Min Ho's Mom or Madam,

274
00:13:38,021 --> 00:13:40,291
just call me "sister," sister-in-law.

275
00:13:40,531 --> 00:13:43,861
It's not like I'm your young unmarried sister-in-law.

276
00:13:44,101 --> 00:13:46,201
What's with the "sister-in-law" business?

277
00:13:46,631 --> 00:13:48,701
Just call me what you always have. Honestly...

278
00:13:48,801 --> 00:13:50,971
No, in a prestigious family like ours,

279
00:13:51,041 --> 00:13:53,711
even our titles must be proper and elegant.

280
00:13:54,011 --> 00:13:57,011
When in Rome, you follow Roman law. What are you talking about?

281
00:13:57,141 --> 00:13:58,911
Just call each other whatever you're comfortable with.

282
00:13:59,181 --> 00:14:02,511
I'm sure the titles will sort themselves out over time.

283
00:14:03,051 --> 00:14:05,151
So, what's all this?

284
00:14:05,351 --> 00:14:08,421
Yes, I brought these to make cold noodles for lunch.

285
00:14:08,491 --> 00:14:09,521
My goodness, Kang Yeon Ja.

286
00:14:09,861 --> 00:14:12,761
I mean, you know how to make cold noodles?

287
00:14:13,361 --> 00:14:16,361
I guess the apple doesn't fall far from the tree.

288
00:14:16,861 --> 00:14:18,661
Mother, I heard you used to work...

289
00:14:18,731 --> 00:14:20,501
in a construction site cafeteria kitchen?

290
00:14:20,871 --> 00:14:23,101
And it seems the daughter inherited that talent...

291
00:14:23,171 --> 00:14:25,401
As soon as the Chairman is up,

292
00:14:25,401 --> 00:14:28,111
- I'll start boiling the noodles. - Yes, please do.

293
00:14:28,711 --> 00:14:32,411
By the way, when can I see all my grandchildren?

294
00:14:32,911 --> 00:14:34,211
Did you find out when they're available?

295
00:14:34,281 --> 00:14:37,121
Yes, I asked my youngest daughter today.

296
00:14:37,251 --> 00:14:38,951
She said she'll coordinate with her brother to find a time.

297
00:14:39,181 --> 00:14:43,791
- The one who quit med school? - Yes.

298
00:14:44,021 --> 00:14:46,491
Oh, I want to see my great-granddaughter soon too.

299
00:14:47,461 --> 00:14:50,561
Do you think your son and his wife will get back together?

300
00:14:50,661 --> 00:14:53,301
It seems you have a lot to talk about,

301
00:14:53,371 --> 00:14:54,971
so I'll go back inside.

302
00:14:55,071 --> 00:14:58,771
- Come out when noodles are done. - Yes, sister-in-law.

303
00:14:59,501 --> 00:15:02,111
Oh, have you set a date?

304
00:15:02,811 --> 00:15:05,011
For the Chairman's living funeral.

305
00:15:05,741 --> 00:15:09,211
I'll help you prepare, so please don't overdo it.

306
00:15:09,581 --> 00:15:10,651
Okay, let's do that.

307
00:15:11,821 --> 00:15:13,651
Gosh, this feels like a dream.

308
00:15:14,191 --> 00:15:17,661
I can't believe I am standing face to face to you like this.

309
00:15:22,831 --> 00:15:25,501
It's like a reunion of separated families, isn't it?

310
00:15:25,601 --> 00:15:28,201
What? Bring everyone home, including the great-granddaughter?

311
00:15:36,741 --> 00:15:37,741
Are you busy?

312
00:15:38,711 --> 00:15:40,681
Why? Did something happen again?

313
00:15:41,151 --> 00:15:44,581
There's always something. Kang Yeon Ja is here...

314
00:15:44,821 --> 00:15:47,221
all cosy with your mother, holding her hands.

315
00:15:47,751 --> 00:15:50,061
Do not do anything to upset them.

316
00:15:50,661 --> 00:15:53,961
I swore to Father that I would never do anything foolish again,

317
00:15:53,961 --> 00:15:56,291
so you cannot be the one to ruin it.

318
00:15:56,431 --> 00:15:58,161
Whatever.

319
00:15:58,361 --> 00:16:01,001
Lately, I do not know what my place is in this house.

320
00:16:01,301 --> 00:16:02,801
I mean, it is not like the fixed stone...

321
00:16:02,871 --> 00:16:04,801
is pushing out the one that rolled in. Seriously...

322
00:16:04,871 --> 00:16:06,841
Wrong, wrong, wrong again.

323
00:16:07,211 --> 00:16:09,341
The stone that rolls in pushes out the fixed stone.

324
00:16:09,671 --> 00:16:11,511
Eun Su Jung. Crystal.

325
00:16:12,081 --> 00:16:14,251
Please, let's just compose ourselves.

326
00:16:15,851 --> 00:16:18,081
I am hanging up. Come in.

327
00:16:19,151 --> 00:16:20,151
Oh my word.

328
00:16:20,721 --> 00:16:23,491
I mean, what exactly does he want me to be discreet about?

329
00:16:23,621 --> 00:16:26,061
Other than blabbing about the DNA test,

330
00:16:26,061 --> 00:16:29,231
what else have I done wrong? Unbelievable.

331
00:16:29,691 --> 00:16:30,701
Darn it.

332
00:16:33,631 --> 00:16:36,771
Well, you see, for some time now,

333
00:16:37,271 --> 00:16:39,971
I have caused you some unreasonable trouble,

334
00:16:40,241 --> 00:16:42,541
and I want to offer my sincere apologies.

335
00:16:43,171 --> 00:16:44,181
I am sorry.

336
00:16:44,911 --> 00:16:46,381
You will accept my apology, will you not?

337
00:16:48,081 --> 00:16:50,421
I would have to know what specifically...

338
00:16:50,421 --> 00:16:51,651
you are apologising for...

339
00:16:53,151 --> 00:16:54,891
For this and that. All sorts of things.

340
00:16:56,121 --> 00:16:58,821
You see, now that things have come to this,

341
00:16:58,891 --> 00:17:00,861
I want to accept you, Secretary Jo, as my brother-in-law...

342
00:17:00,931 --> 00:17:03,261
and get along with you from now on.

343
00:17:03,601 --> 00:17:07,601
You know, without being difficult, but reasonably and properly.

344
00:17:08,701 --> 00:17:11,001
It is good for us to get along, but...

345
00:17:12,901 --> 00:17:14,371
What is it you really want to say?

346
00:17:15,841 --> 00:17:18,911
Well, about the proposal my father made last time...

347
00:17:19,011 --> 00:17:21,181
The matter of being added to the family registry.

348
00:17:21,181 --> 00:17:23,051
Have you reached a decision?

349
00:17:23,981 --> 00:17:26,051
No, not yet.

350
00:17:26,581 --> 00:17:29,151
Not yet? What is taking so long to decide?

351
00:17:29,221 --> 00:17:31,161
It is a simple yes or no question.

352
00:17:32,321 --> 00:17:33,461
Traditionally,

353
00:17:33,831 --> 00:17:35,491
a family registry is for blood relatives.

354
00:17:35,761 --> 00:17:37,861
No matter what anyone says, only Father's blood relatives...

355
00:17:37,961 --> 00:17:40,131
are qualified to be on that registry, don't you think?

356
00:17:41,031 --> 00:17:43,201
That is a decision for my wife to make,

357
00:17:43,271 --> 00:17:45,571
so I do not believe it is my place to answer.

358
00:17:46,041 --> 00:17:50,441
Seriously? I cannot understand it. The great Jo Sung Jun...

359
00:17:50,511 --> 00:17:52,181
cannot even make one simple decision.

360
00:17:53,041 --> 00:17:55,081
Are you henpecked, Secretary Jo? Like me?

361
00:17:56,921 --> 00:17:59,451
There is something I am curious about.

362
00:18:01,621 --> 00:18:03,021
Was there some special reason...

363
00:18:03,591 --> 00:18:05,391
why you adopted Team Leader Ko?

364
00:18:07,561 --> 00:18:08,561
What did you say?

365
00:18:08,961 --> 00:18:11,161
You seem to value bloodlines more than anyone,

366
00:18:11,231 --> 00:18:12,931
and there is General Director Ko. So why...

367
00:18:13,831 --> 00:18:15,871
did you end up adopting Team Leader Ko?

368
00:18:16,531 --> 00:18:18,041
I suddenly became curious.

369
00:18:19,041 --> 00:18:20,041
Well...

370
00:18:21,211 --> 00:18:23,881
Well, that is because I am a devoted son.

371
00:18:24,211 --> 00:18:26,181
If my father told me to die,

372
00:18:26,181 --> 00:18:28,551
I am the kind of person who would pretend to die.

373
00:18:29,481 --> 00:18:30,521
I guess you did not know.

374
00:18:30,981 --> 00:18:32,481
Is that all?

375
00:18:32,481 --> 00:18:34,691
Well... What else would there be?

376
00:18:34,691 --> 00:18:35,691
Unbelievable.

377
00:18:36,391 --> 00:18:37,621
What are you doing? You can go now.

378
00:18:39,021 --> 00:18:40,021
Yes, sir.

379
00:18:40,131 --> 00:18:41,791
(Gangsu Construction)

380
00:18:41,861 --> 00:18:43,861
- Well then. - Yes.

381
00:18:47,731 --> 00:18:51,401
What is with that guy? I tried to get along with him...

382
00:18:51,471 --> 00:18:54,471
and even extended an olive branch, but now he is acting up again.

383
00:18:56,981 --> 00:18:59,181
Does he know something?

384
00:19:00,151 --> 00:19:01,381
He was arrested and taken into custody?

385
00:19:02,281 --> 00:19:05,981
Where exactly was Jung Dong Pal arrested?

386
00:19:06,991 --> 00:19:08,251
In front of CS convenience store?

387
00:19:09,221 --> 00:19:10,361
Yes, I understand.

388
00:19:10,721 --> 00:19:13,391
No, I was just curious.

389
00:19:14,131 --> 00:19:15,131
Yes.

390
00:19:20,331 --> 00:19:21,801
Oh, General Director Ko, where are you now?

391
00:19:22,731 --> 00:19:25,771
You are? I'll head over. Okay.

392
00:19:27,641 --> 00:19:29,211
Can you give me more details?

393
00:19:29,711 --> 00:19:31,141
Things were so chaotic that day.

394
00:19:32,211 --> 00:19:33,781
So you're saying Seung Ri called the police...

395
00:19:33,781 --> 00:19:35,211
and was then taken hostage?

396
00:19:35,681 --> 00:19:39,321
- In front of CS convenience store. - Yes.

397
00:19:40,291 --> 00:19:41,491
But why do you ask?

398
00:19:42,291 --> 00:19:44,521
I thought something seemed strange that day too.

399
00:19:45,161 --> 00:19:46,161
By any chance,

400
00:19:46,491 --> 00:19:49,291
is there some kind of connection between that man and Seung Ri?

401
00:19:49,491 --> 00:19:51,231
No, that's impossible.

402
00:19:52,001 --> 00:19:53,601
I didn't think much of it at the time,

403
00:19:54,301 --> 00:19:56,371
but it seems like what Seung Ri did was far too dangerous.

404
00:19:57,271 --> 00:19:59,701
That bastard didn't threaten my daughter...

405
00:19:59,771 --> 00:20:01,511
with a dangerous weapon, did he?

406
00:20:02,041 --> 00:20:04,041
I'm not entirely sure,

407
00:20:04,581 --> 00:20:07,911
but the police and I burst in right as she was taken hostage,

408
00:20:07,981 --> 00:20:09,051
so she was freed right away.

409
00:20:13,121 --> 00:20:14,121
Chief Seo.

410
00:20:15,291 --> 00:20:18,321
- Are you all right? - Yes, of course I am.

411
00:20:19,061 --> 00:20:21,361
Thank you. If it weren't for you, General Director Ko...

412
00:20:22,591 --> 00:20:26,131
(General Director Ko Min Ho)

413
00:20:28,271 --> 00:20:29,831
Chief Seo, too? Why?

414
00:20:30,601 --> 00:20:31,971
I think there's something more to this.

415
00:20:33,271 --> 00:20:34,271
Dad.

416
00:20:35,311 --> 00:20:36,841
- Oh. - What are you doing here?

417
00:20:37,711 --> 00:20:38,711
Well...

418
00:20:40,351 --> 00:20:43,251
- Want dinner with me tonight? - Eat out?

419
00:20:44,551 --> 00:20:45,551
Yes, that sounds great.

420
00:20:45,621 --> 00:20:47,351
I'll wait for you in the lobby after work.

421
00:20:47,421 --> 00:20:48,891
Okay, see you later.

422
00:20:56,691 --> 00:20:59,331
What brings you here without calling?

423
00:21:00,631 --> 00:21:01,671
Well,

424
00:21:01,971 --> 00:21:06,041
being at home just stresses me out. Who else do I have?

425
00:21:06,541 --> 00:21:08,511
You're my one and only best friend.

426
00:21:08,641 --> 00:21:09,741
Best friend? Please.

427
00:21:10,311 --> 00:21:11,781
I'm only your best friend when you need something.

428
00:21:12,811 --> 00:21:13,811
Have a seat.

429
00:21:15,711 --> 00:21:17,721
Kang Yeon Ja is at my house right now.

430
00:21:18,351 --> 00:21:20,321
That mother and daughter are so incredibly close,

431
00:21:20,621 --> 00:21:22,051
it's honestly sickening.

432
00:21:22,321 --> 00:21:24,021
I can't even stand to look at them.

433
00:21:24,661 --> 00:21:26,491
Why would you find that sickening?

434
00:21:27,091 --> 00:21:29,191
They're a mother and daughter who just reunited after 50 years.

435
00:21:29,461 --> 00:21:30,901
Of course they're going to be emotional.

436
00:21:31,401 --> 00:21:33,261
Be honest with me.

437
00:21:33,871 --> 00:21:35,401
Who is it? Me or Kang Yeon Ja?

438
00:21:35,771 --> 00:21:39,041
Excuse me? What kind of question is that?

439
00:21:39,101 --> 00:21:43,741
Lately, you've been icing me out and taking Kang Yeon Ja's side.

440
00:21:44,081 --> 00:21:46,381
We even have a 25-year friendship.

441
00:21:46,441 --> 00:21:48,611
I am not on Kang Yeon Ja's side.

442
00:21:49,211 --> 00:21:50,251
That's ridiculous.

443
00:21:51,751 --> 00:21:53,151
Actually, the other day,

444
00:21:53,751 --> 00:21:55,751
I had a huge fight with Kang Yeon Ja.

445
00:21:55,951 --> 00:21:58,921
What? Really? Why?

446
00:21:59,221 --> 00:22:00,221
You see,

447
00:22:00,531 --> 00:22:02,661
I can let other things slide, but when it comes to my child...

448
00:22:03,661 --> 00:22:06,831
She said our Seung Woo looks like a gigolo,

449
00:22:07,001 --> 00:22:08,271
- Oh my. - and then she started...

450
00:22:08,271 --> 00:22:11,041
questioning his upbringing and hit him on the back.

451
00:22:11,371 --> 00:22:13,201
How could I just stand by and watch?

452
00:22:13,971 --> 00:22:14,971
I tell you,

453
00:22:15,411 --> 00:22:18,781
if it wasn't Kang Yeon Ja, that day I would have...

454
00:22:19,311 --> 00:22:23,781
Even if she is the Madam's daughter, that's too much.

455
00:22:24,381 --> 00:22:28,251
My goodness. That girl is so strange.

456
00:22:28,491 --> 00:22:32,491
What's wrong with Seung Woo? He's kind, handsome, and cute.

457
00:22:32,561 --> 00:22:33,561
He has good manners too.

458
00:22:34,231 --> 00:22:36,391
But why did she hit Seung Woo?

459
00:22:36,461 --> 00:22:39,931
Her youngest daughter is working on a project with Seung Woo,

460
00:22:39,931 --> 00:22:41,731
and she got drenched with water.

461
00:22:41,801 --> 00:22:42,931
So she misunderstood when she saw her...

462
00:22:42,931 --> 00:22:44,171
wearing his clothes.

463
00:22:44,671 --> 00:22:49,571
Oh my gosh. That woman is ridiculous, right?

464
00:22:51,941 --> 00:22:53,751
How did you think of coming to a place like this?

465
00:22:54,651 --> 00:22:58,051
Just because. We're together at work and at home,

466
00:22:58,121 --> 00:23:00,621
so I felt like we haven't had a proper date.

467
00:23:00,851 --> 00:23:03,521
What exactly is a proper date?

468
00:23:04,121 --> 00:23:07,191
For me, every single moment with you has been special, Eun Ae.

469
00:23:08,961 --> 00:23:12,231
At first, I thought you had a real talent for saying hurtful things.

470
00:23:12,401 --> 00:23:14,671
Right, what did you say to me?

471
00:23:14,671 --> 00:23:16,031
You asked if I was...

472
00:23:16,101 --> 00:23:18,171
getting tutored to be unlikeable, didn't you?

473
00:23:18,841 --> 00:23:19,871
Did you know?

474
00:23:20,611 --> 00:23:23,881
That among all those stars we see up there,

475
00:23:24,211 --> 00:23:26,141
many of them have already disappeared.

476
00:23:27,311 --> 00:23:29,051
Of course, I know that.

477
00:23:30,051 --> 00:23:33,621
It takes light several light-years to reach Earth.

478
00:23:34,221 --> 00:23:35,951
Even stars that have already disappeared,

479
00:23:36,551 --> 00:23:38,521
as long as we're looking at them like this,

480
00:23:38,991 --> 00:23:40,591
they still exist in a way, right?

481
00:23:42,091 --> 00:23:45,201
It's the same for your father, Team Leader Ko.

482
00:23:47,831 --> 00:23:48,871
What I mean is,

483
00:23:49,471 --> 00:23:52,601
your father, like those stars,

484
00:23:53,401 --> 00:23:56,941
is watching over you from somewhere.

485
00:23:59,941 --> 00:24:02,651
You sound just like my father.

486
00:24:03,651 --> 00:24:04,651
Pardon?

487
00:24:06,721 --> 00:24:09,651
My mother passed away right after I was born,

488
00:24:11,021 --> 00:24:12,421
and my dad always used to say that.

489
00:24:13,421 --> 00:24:15,491
That my mom became a star in the sky...

490
00:24:16,761 --> 00:24:18,431
and that she was watching over me.

491
00:24:19,001 --> 00:24:20,601
I'd forgotten about it for a while as I grew up.

492
00:24:22,431 --> 00:24:24,941
I feel like I said the wrong thing.

493
00:24:25,901 --> 00:24:26,901
No, you didn't.

494
00:24:27,771 --> 00:24:29,611
The story I really wanted to tell...

495
00:24:30,411 --> 00:24:31,641
was about my father.

496
00:24:33,041 --> 00:24:36,011
I just didn't have anyone I could open up to about it.

497
00:24:37,011 --> 00:24:39,021
It's not something I could talk to my grandfather about.

498
00:24:39,081 --> 00:24:43,121
Then from now on, you can tell me anything.

499
00:24:43,351 --> 00:24:44,361
Everything.

500
00:24:45,221 --> 00:24:46,321
On my birthday,

501
00:24:47,291 --> 00:24:49,131
I blew out my candles and made a wish.

502
00:24:49,961 --> 00:24:51,101
I told him...

503
00:24:52,461 --> 00:24:53,461
that I wished...

504
00:24:54,301 --> 00:24:55,901
I could live happily with him...

505
00:24:56,871 --> 00:24:59,541
until the end of the world.

506
00:25:01,571 --> 00:25:02,571
But...

507
00:25:03,641 --> 00:25:05,181
my father passed away that day.

508
00:25:07,681 --> 00:25:08,781
So after that,

509
00:25:10,111 --> 00:25:11,821
I've lived my life...

510
00:25:12,321 --> 00:25:13,421
with my heart tightly closed.

511
00:25:16,091 --> 00:25:17,091
But...

512
00:25:18,361 --> 00:25:19,621
the me inside is telling me...

513
00:25:21,361 --> 00:25:22,731
to open that door.

514
00:25:26,531 --> 00:25:27,971
Aren't you scared?

515
00:25:29,331 --> 00:25:32,641
It might be such a painful memory...

516
00:25:33,471 --> 00:25:35,841
that you've kept it hidden away.

517
00:25:35,971 --> 00:25:37,011
I'm scared.

518
00:25:37,681 --> 00:25:38,681
Very.

519
00:25:40,141 --> 00:25:41,551
But I'm going to try to open it.

520
00:25:43,011 --> 00:25:44,321
Whatever it may be,

521
00:25:45,621 --> 00:25:47,421
I won't run away from it anymore.

522
00:25:48,551 --> 00:25:52,091
You may be facing the memory alone,

523
00:25:53,391 --> 00:25:55,061
but don't forget that by your side,

524
00:25:55,891 --> 00:26:00,771
there are people who genuinely care for and love you.

525
00:26:02,031 --> 00:26:03,801
Your grandfather, your grandmother,

526
00:26:04,801 --> 00:26:05,941
and me too.

527
00:26:07,871 --> 00:26:08,871
I...

528
00:26:09,541 --> 00:26:12,181
will always be by your side.

529
00:26:14,151 --> 00:26:16,011
Without leaving you for one moment.

530
00:26:17,481 --> 00:26:18,481
Always.

531
00:26:21,391 --> 00:26:22,721
Can I have your hand?

532
00:26:23,591 --> 00:26:26,521
Pardon? My hand?

533
00:26:54,591 --> 00:26:55,591
Team Leader Ko.

534
00:26:56,621 --> 00:26:58,291
I got this a long time ago,

535
00:26:59,361 --> 00:27:00,761
but I've only just now worked up the courage.

536
00:27:02,761 --> 00:27:03,831
From now on...

537
00:27:05,361 --> 00:27:07,271
I'm going to see this through to the end with you, Jo Eun Ae.

538
00:27:10,371 --> 00:27:12,201
Does that mean...

539
00:27:14,141 --> 00:27:17,781
you're not planning on going back to the States?

540
00:27:19,081 --> 00:27:20,141
Maybe.

541
00:27:21,211 --> 00:27:22,251
Or...

542
00:27:23,511 --> 00:27:24,951
I could go with you.

543
00:27:37,161 --> 00:27:38,231
Will you...

544
00:27:39,631 --> 00:27:40,931
come with me...

545
00:27:42,801 --> 00:27:45,971
until the end of the world?

546
00:27:49,011 --> 00:27:51,441
Yes, I will.

547
00:27:53,211 --> 00:27:56,851
Wherever that is, I will go with you...

548
00:27:58,221 --> 00:27:59,281
to the very end.

549
00:28:28,181 --> 00:28:30,781
(Our Happy Days)
